# .assetsignore - what the STAGING Worker does not upload. gitignore syntax, read by wrangler
# from the assets directory (the repo root, see wrangler.jsonc). Infrastructure, not app.
#
# Everything tracked in the repo IS served, on purpose: staging must answer every path the way
# GitHub Pages answers it for release, and Pages serves the whole branch. Only two kinds of
# path are excluded - git's own store, and the gitignored local tooling that never reaches
# Cloudflare's checkout but does exist on this box, so a local `wrangler deploy --dry-run`
# walks the same tree the build does.
.git/
node_modules/
.wrangler/
/graphify-out/
/.omc/
/.superpowers/
/docs/superpowers/
/test/test-results/
/test/playwright-report/
